.TH KISA-CCE-COLLECT 8 "2026-09-03" "KISA CCE Linux Scanner" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
kisa-cce-collect \- collect live runtime evidence for an offline KISA CCE scan
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kisa-cce-collect
.BI \-\-output-dir " PATH"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kisa-cce-collect
captures a bounded snapshot of live Linux identity, systemd units, listeners,
mounts, firewall state, and time synchronization state.
The resulting owner-only directory can be supplied to
.BR kisa-cce-scan (8)
with
.BR \-\-evidence-bundle .
.PP
The collector must run as root on the live system immediately before creating
the corresponding offline filesystem snapshot.
It does not create an archive, probe remote services, refresh package metadata,
or collect authentication secrets.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-output-dir " PATH"
Create or use an empty absolute directory for the evidence bundle.
The directory must be root-owned, must have mode 0700, and must not be a
symbolic link.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the evidence schema version and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
Every terminal line uses a dmesg-style prefix with six fractional uptime
digits. This applies to help, version, errors, warnings, and the successful
bundle path. A safe process-time or zero fallback is used when
.I /proc/uptime
is unavailable. On success, the collector prints:
.PP
.EX
[    12.345678] kisa-cce-collect: evidence_bundle=/absolute/path
.EE
.PP
The directory contains a strict manifest, SHA-256 checksums, host identity,
normalized service and listener tables, raw mount information, firewall state,
and time synchronization state.
All files use mode 0600 and all directories use mode 0700.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The bundle was finalized successfully.
Optional runtime sources can still be marked partial or unavailable in the
manifest.
.TP
.B 2
Invocation, identity collection, output security, or finalization failed.
.TP
.B 130
The process received SIGINT.
.TP
.B 143
The process received SIGTERM.
.SH SECURITY
The bundle contains sensitive infrastructure metadata.
Store and transfer it as security assessment data.
SHA-256 checksums detect modification after capture but do not authenticate the
collector or transport by themselves.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kisa-cce-scan (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR ss (8),
.BR proc_pid_mountinfo (5)
